1. **Convert the percentage to a fraction:**  
   0.044% = 0.044 / 100 = 0.0044

2. **Interpret the (w/v) notation:**  
   (w/v) means weight of solute (in grams) per volume of solution (in milliliters).  
   Thus, 0.044% (w/v) means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride per 100 mL of Phos-Flur Rinse.

3. **Calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL:**  
   If 100 mL contains 0.044 g, then 1 mL contains 0.044 / 100 = 0.00044 g.  
   Thus, 10 mL contains 0.044 × 100 = 0.44 g of sodium fluoride.

4. **Convert grams to milligrams:**  
   1 g = 1000 mg  
