The most common bifurcation lesions are:
- **True bifurcation lesions** (e.g., LAD-LCx, RCA-LAD, LAD-RCA).
- **Non-true bifurcation lesions** (e.g., LCx-LAD, RCA-LCx).

The most common bifurcation lesion is the **LAD-LCx bifurcation**, followed by the **RCA-LAD bifurcation**.

$\boxed{\text{The LAD-LCx bifurcation is associated with higher rates of procedural complications during PCI of the parent vessel.}}$
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

