   \[
   \text{Mass of NaCl} = \text{Total mass of sea salt} \times \text{Percentage of NaCl}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Mass of NaCl} = 5 \text{ g} \times 0.85 = 4.25 \text{ g}
   \]

2. **Interpretation of Gravimetric Analysis:**
   Gravimetric analysis involves weighing the solid NaCl after it has been isolated from the sea salt. The answer (4.25 g) is the mass of NaCl that would be obtained after the gravimetric analysis process.

3. **Final Answer:**
   The amount of NaCl that can be obtained from the 5 grams of sea salt is \(\boxed{4.25 \text{ g}}\).
