We use Hess''s law:  
\[ \Delta H = \Delta H_{\text{product}} - \Delta H_{\text{reactants}} \]  
1. **Enthalpy of formation of the product, [Fe(4]2−**:  
   \[ \Delta H_{\text{Fe}^{2+}\text{Cl}_4}^{2-} = -392 \, \text{kJ/mol} \]  
2. **Enthalapy of hydration of Fe²⁺ ions**:  
   \[ \Delta H_{\text{H}_2\text{O} \text{Fe}^{2+}} = -340 \, \text{kJ/mol} \]  
3. **Enthalapy of hydration of Cl⁻ ions**:  
   \[ \Delta H_{\text{H}_2\text{O} \text{Cl}^-} = -381 \, \text{kJ/mol} \]  
4. **Substitute into Hess’s law**:  
   \[ \Delta H = \Delta H_{\text{Fe}^{2+}\text{Cl}_4}^{2+} + 6\Delta H_{\text{H}_2\text{O}} + 2\Delta H_{\text{Cl}^-} - \Delta H_{\text{Fe}^{2+}} - 6\Delta H_{\text{H}_2\text{O}} \]  
