- Guanines (G): 25 (from the first strand) + 25 (from the complementary strand) = 50
- Cytosines (C): 30 (from the first strand) + 30 (from the complementary strand) = 60
- Thymines (T): 22 (from the first strand) + 22 (from the complementary strand) = 44

Thus, the complete double-stranded DNA molecule contains:
- 40 A
