   \]
   \[
   \text{Weight of sulphur} = 1.6375 \text{ mol} \times 32 \text{ g/mol} = 52.5 \text{ g}
   \]

3. **Calculate the weight of residual gases:**
   The total weight of the air is 250 g. The weight of sulphur burned is 52.5 g, and the weight of SO₂ produced is equal to the weight of oxygen consumed (since sulphur and oxygen combine completely).
   \[
   \text{Weight of SO}_2 = 52.5 \text{ g}
   \]
   The remaining gases are nitrogen and other trace gases.
   \[
   \text{Weight of residual gases} = 250 \text{ g} - 52.5 \text{ g} - 52.5 \text{ g} = 145 \text{ g}
   \]

