For the given reaction:

\[
\text{ΔH = ΔH₀ (Ca(OH)2(s]) - ΔH₀ (CaO(s]) - ΔH₀ (H2O(l])}
\]

Substitute the given values:

\[
\text{ΔH} = (-986.2 \text{ kJ/mol}) - (-635.1 \text{ kJ/mol}) - (-285.8 \text{ kJ/mol})
\]

\[
\text{ΔH} = -986.2 + 635.1 + 285.8 = -165.3 \text{ kJ/mol}
\]

Thus, the standard enthalpy change for the reaction is \(\boxed{-165.3 \text{ kJ/mol}}\).
