We use Hess''s law:  
\[ \Delta H = \Delta H_{\text{product}} - \Delta H_{\text{reactants}} \]  
1. **Enthalpy of formation of the product, [Fe(4]2−**:  
   \[ \Delta H_{\text{Fe}^{2+}\text{Cl}_4}^{2-} = -392 \, \text{kJ/mol} \]  
2. **Enthalapy of hydration of Fe²⁺ ions**:  
