For each component, the reliability is \( P(T > t) = S(t) = 1 - \lambda t \), where \( T \) is the lifetime of the component.  

For independent components, the reliability of the system depends on the reliability of its components.  

---

### a) Serial Structure  
In a serial (series) series, the system fails if any component fails.  

If the system consists of \( n \) independent components with reliability \( S_1(t) = S_2(t) = S_3(t) = S_n(t) = 1 - \lambda t \), the system reliability is the product of the components' reliability:  

\[
