Thus, for \( n \) components in a series series:  
\[
R_S(t) = ( 1 - \lambda t ) \times n = 1 - \lambda t \times n = 1 - \lambda n t \]  

For \( n \) components, the system lifetime \( T_S \) is the sum of the lifetimes of the components.  
\[
P(T_S > t) = 1 - \lambda t \times n = 1 - \lambda n t
\]

