Since it takes him 20 minutes to reach the destination, the distance to the friend's house is:
$5200 \text{ cm/min} \times 20 \text{ min} = 104,000 \text{ cm}$.

Now, we calculate the speed of Lucy.
Lucy walks at 90 steps per minute, and each step is 55 cm long.
So, her speed is $90 \text{ steps/min} \times 55 \text{ cm/step} = 4950 \text{ cm/min}$.

To find the time it takes Lucy to reach the friend's house, we divide the distance by her speed:
Time = Distance / Speed
Time = $104,000 \text{ cm} / 4950 \text{ cm/min} = \frac{104,000}{4950} \text{ min}$.
