A cylinder contains 2 moles of an ideal gas at an initial pressure of 2 atm and an initial volume of 4L. The gas expands isothermally until its volume becomes 8L. Calculate the work done by the gas during the expansion process.<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The work done by the gas during an isothermal expansion is given by the formula:  
\[
W = -PV_1 P_1 \left( \frac{1}{P_2 - P_1} \right)
\]  
However, for an ideal gas, the ideal gas law is given as \( P(V) = nRT \), where \( n \) is the number of moles, \( R \) is the gas constant, and \( T \)) is the temperature.  
For an isothermal process, \( T \) is constant, and \( P_1 V_1 = n R T = P_2 V_2 \).  
Thus, \( P_2 = \frac{P_1 V_1}{V_2} \).  
The work done is given by:  
\[
W = - n R T \ln \left( \frac{V_2}{V_1} \).  
\]  
Given:  
- Number of moles, \( n = 2 \)  
- Initial pressure, \( P_1 = 2 \, \text{atm} \)  
- Initial volume, \( V_1 = 4 \, \text{L} \)  
- Final volume, \( V_2 = 8 \, \text{L} \)  
- Gas is ideal, so \( P_1 V_1 = n R T \)  
- Isothermic, so \( T \) is constant.  

First, calculate the change in pressure:  
\[
P_2 = \frac{P_1 V_1}{V_2} = \frac{2 \, \text{atm} \times 4 \, \text{L}}{8 \, \text{L}} = 1 \, \text{atm}.  
\]  
Now, calculate the work done:  
\[
W = - P_1 (V_2 - V_1) = - 2 \, \text{atm} (8 \, \text{L} - 4 \, \text{L}) = - 2 \, \text{atm} \times 4 \, \text{L} = - 8 \, \text{J}.  
\]  
Alternatively, using the formula \( W = - n R T \ln \left( \frac{V_2}{V_1} \right \), we first need to find \( n R T \).  
\[
n R T = P_1 V_1 = 2 \, \text{atm} \times 4 \, \text{L} = 8 \, \text{J} \, \text{atm} = 8 \times 100.22 \, \text{J} = 801.16 \, \text{J}.  
\]  
Substituting into the formula:  
\[
W = - 801.16 \, \text{J} \ln \left( \frac{8}{4} \right) = - 801.16 \, \text{J} \ln (2) = - 801.16 \, \text{J} \times 0.594 \approx -454 \, \text{J}.  
\]  
However, the correct formula for the work is:  
\[
W = - P_1 (V_2 - V_1) = - 2 \, \text{atm} ( 8 - 4 ) = - 2 \, \text{atm} \times 4 \, \text{L}",relevance,"# Task Description
