   η = 1 - (P₂/P₁^(k/(n)))
   where:
   - η = efficiency
   - P₂ = pressure at the end of compression
   - P₁ = pressure at the beginning of compression
   - k = adiabatic constant (for air, k ≈ 1.4)
   - n = number of molecules (1 for air)

