The current through the circuit is \( i(t) = 0.2e^{-4t} \, \text{A} \).
The current is given by \( i = \frac{V}{C} \), where \( V \) is the voltage across the capacitor and \( C \) is the capacitance.
From the given circuit, the voltage \( v(t) \) is the voltage across the capacitor, and the current \( i(t)) \) is the current through the capacitor.
