At \( t = 0 \), \( i(0) = 0.2e^{-4(0}) = 0.2 \, \text{A} \).
Thus, \( 0.2 = \frac{10}{C} \), so \( C = \frac{10}{0.2} = 50 \, \text{V}. \)
The energy stored in the capacitor at \( t = 0 \) is:
\[
E_{0} = \frac{1}{2} C V(0)^2 = \frac{1}{2} (50)(10)^2 = \frac{1}{2} (50)(100) = 2500 \, \text{J}.
\]

Thus, the initial energy in the capacitor is \( 2500 \, \text{J} \).

Final Answer:
\[
E_{0} = 2500 \, \text{J}.
