This reaction occurs at the cathode, where the zinc electrode is the electrode where the oxidation occurs. The anode is the lead electrode, where the reduction occurs. The overall reaction is:  
\[ \text{Zn} + 2 \text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{Zn}_2\text{OH}_2 + \text{H}_2 \text{ (gas)} \]  

**Explanation:**  
- The lead electrode (anode) oxidizes to form solid $\text{Pb}^2^+$ ions, which migrate into the electrolyte.  
- The hydrogen ions ($\text{H}^2^+$) in the electrolyte react with the $\text{Pb}^2+}$ ions to form solid $\text{Pb}^2^+$ ions, which migrate into the electrolyte.  
