- The hydrogen ions ($\text{H}_2\text{O}$) in the electrolyte react with the $\text{Ag}_2\text{OH}_2$ ions to form solid $\text{Ag}_2\text{OH}_2}$ ions, which migrate into the electrolyte.  

The overall reaction is:  
\[ \text{Pb} + 2 \text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{Pb}_2\text{H}_4 + \text{H}_2 \text{ (gas)} \]  

