2. **Water's latent heat:**  
   The latent heat of vaporization at 220°C is \(L = 1858.5 \, \text{kJ/kg}\).  

3. **Heat transferred to the water:**  
   The heat \(Q\) transferred from the gas to the water is equal to the latent heat of the water vaporized:  
   \[
   Q = 1 \, \text{ kg} \times 1885.5 \, \text{kJ/kg} = 1885.5 \, \text{kJ}
