A particle of mass 30 kg is subjected to a force of 32 N. Calculate the acceleration of the particle.
</USER_REQUEST>

<GROUND_TRUTH>
Using Newton's second law of motion:
\[ F = ma \]
where:
- \( F = 32 \, \text{N} \) (force applied)
- \( m = 30 \, \text{kg} \) (mass of the particle)

Rearranging to solve for acceleration \( a \):
\[ a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{32}{30} \]

Simplifying the fraction:
\[ a = \frac{16}{15} \, \text{m/s}^2 \]

Thus, the acceleration of the particle is \(\boxed{\dfrac{16}{15} \, \text{m/s}^2}\).
</GROUND_TRUTH>

